     ccuurrrreennttllyy nnoo lloooopp ddeetteeccttiioonn iinn ppllaaccee..

MMOODDUULLEE OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     Some PAM library functions may alter their behavior when called by a ser‐
     vice module if certain module options were specified, regardless of
     whether the module itself accords them any importance.  One such option
     is ddeebbuugg, which causes the dispatcher to enable debugging messages before
     calling each service function, and disable them afterwards (unless they
     were already enabled).  Other special options include:

     aauutthhttookk__pprroommpptt=_p_r_o_m_p_t, oollddaauutthhttookk__pprroommpptt=_p_r_o_m_p_t, uusseerr__pprroommpptt=_p_r_o_m_p_t
                   These options can be used to override the prompts used by
                   pam_get_authtok(3) and pam_get_user(3).

     eecchhoo__ppaassss     This option controls whether pam_get_authtok(3) will allow
                   the user to see what they are typing.

     ttrryy__ffiirrsstt__ppaassss, uussee__ffiirrsstt__ppaassss
                   These options control pam_get_authtok(3)'s use of cached
                   authentication tokens.

